(load "carp-coordinator.carp")

(Project.config "title" "carp-coordinator")
(Project.config "docs-directory" "./docs/")
(Project.config "docs-logo" "")
(Project.config "docs-url" "https://github.com/carpentry-org/carp-coordinator")
(Project.config "docs-styling" "../style.css")
(Project.config "docs-prelude" "An event system for Carp, in three layers that
can be used separately or together.

```
(load \"git@github.com:carpentry-org/carp-coordinator@master\")
```

### Layers
- [`Dispatcher`](./Dispatcher.html) — the switchboard. handlers subscribe and
  get an id back; `broadcast!` calls each of them synchronously. handlers are
  snapshotted first, so a handler may subscribe or unsubscribe mid-broadcast
  without disturbing the one in flight.
- [`Scheduler`](./Scheduler.html) — the clock. a binary heap of
  [`TimedEvent`](./TimedEvent.html)s ordered by due time, with one-shot and
  periodic tasks and cancellation by id.
- [`Coordinator`](./Coordinator.html) — the two above plus a FIFO queue, driven
  by a throttled run loop. `tick!` drains the queue exhaustively, so events
  raised by handlers run in the same tick.

### Events
Events are whatever type you make them, usually a sumtype. handlers return a
`Result`, and the coordinator counts the failures rather than swallowing them.

```
(deftype AppEvent (Msg [String]) (Stop []))

(let-do [c (Coordinator.new)]
  (Coordinator.subscribe! &c &(fn [ev]
    (match ev
      (AppEvent.Msg s) (do (IO.println s) (Result.Success ()))
      (AppEvent.Stop)  (do (Coordinator.stop! &c) (Result.Success ())))))
  (Coordinator.dispatch! &c (AppEvent.Msg @\"hello\"))
  (Coordinator.schedule! &c (AppEvent.Stop) 1000l)
  (Coordinator.run! &c))
```")

(save-docs TimedEvent Dispatcher Scheduler Coordinator)
; Carp's save-docs hardcodes the index filename as <title>_index.html.
; Rename to docs/index.html.
(defn main []
  (System.system "mv ./docs/carp-coordinator_index.html ./docs/index.html"))
